  "logic": "Screenshots of frontend/e2e/baseline/screens.spec.ts, of the whole page or, for a dialog, of the viewport (Playwright Chromium, the e2e API mocks, clock fixed at 2026-10-28T09:00:00Z, cs-CZ, Europe/Prague, reduced motion, animations off) at 390 and 1280 px wide, 900 px viewport height; a second recording on the same machine gives the same pixels, which the recording script checks, and a comparison run (testing.md) accepts up to 0.2 % of pixels. The PNGs are kept outside the repository, in `stored`. pixelsSha256 is the SHA-256 of the decoded pixels (8-bit RGBA, row by row), so a chunk a file store adds does not change it; bytes is the size as recorded. The digests hold on the recording machine; another browser build renders other pixels, so a differing digest means comparing pixels (testing.md), never recording again.",
